---
import '../../styles/legal.css';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteChrome from '../../components/SiteChrome.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

/* Google's OAuth consent screen asks for a terms link beside the privacy one.
   Kept deliberately short: a wall of boilerplate nobody reads is worse than a
   page that says the few things that are actually true of this app. */
const updated = 'August 2, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Munchview Terms of Service — DeftDay Studio"
  description="The short version: Munchview is free to use, plays videos through YouTube's own player, and makes no claim over anything you watch."
>
  <SiteChrome />
  <div class="sky" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="s1"></span><span class="s2"></span><span class="s3"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="progress" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <main id="main" class="legal">
    <span class="eyebrow">Munchview</span>
    <h1>Short terms,<br /><span class="serif">plainly put.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Munchview finds a video that fits the time you have. These terms cover
      using it. They are short because the app does little that needs governing.
    </p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <section class="legal-block" aria-labelledby="use">
      <h2 id="use">Using the app</h2>
      <p>
        Munchview is free to use. Some conveniences are sold as “Pro”; playback
        itself is never behind a payment, and never will be — YouTube's own
        terms do not permit charging to watch videos in an embedded player.
      </p>
      <p>
        Use it lawfully and do not attempt to break, overload or misuse the
        service. That is the whole of what we ask.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-block" aria-labelledby="youtube">
      <h2 id="youtube">Videos come from other platforms</h2>
      <p>
        Munchview does not host or own any video. Everything plays through the
        platform's own embedded player — YouTube, Dailymotion, Vimeo, Twitch,
        a PeerTube instance, or the Internet Archive — and each platform's own
        terms apply to what happens inside its player.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where YouTube is the platform, you are also bound by the
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube Terms of Service</a>.
        Munchview uses YouTube API Services; Google's
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Privacy Policy</a>
        applies to what Google receives.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Munchview does not ask you to connect an account on any video
        platform.</b> Until 20 August 2026 it could optionally read what you
        had liked or followed on YouTube, Vimeo, Dailymotion or Twitch and show
        each as its own list; that was removed from the app, and Munchview
        holds no account or access token of yours on any of them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-block" aria-labelledby="account">
      <h2 id="account">Your account and your data</h2>
      <p>
        Signing in is optional and exists to carry your preferences to another
        phone. What we store, and how to delete it, is set out in the
        <a href="/munchview/privacy">privacy policy</a>. You can delete
        everything we hold at any time — in the app, or at
        <a href="/munchview/delete-account">deftday.com/munchview/delete-account</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-block" aria-labelledby="asis">
      <h2 id="asis">No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The app is provided as it is. We work to keep it running and correct,
        but we cannot promise it will always be available or that every video it
        suggests will suit you. To the extent the law allows, DeftDay Studio is
        not liable for loss arising from using it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-block" aria-labelledby="changes">
      <h2 id="changes">Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        If these terms change in a way that matters, the date above changes with
        them. Questions:
        <a href="mailto:privacy@deftday.com">privacy@deftday.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>
